{"level":30,"time":1778264911911,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QRjcYuaWjLfELfgFJ13wqd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have the context. Let me summarize what I know:\n\n**Grouping Information:**\n- Grouping ID: `1` (from filename `1.md`)\n- Topic: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n- This is about clearance requirements between overhead electric distribution/transmission facilities and proposed site features (buildings, fences, retaining walls, driveways, parking, etc.)\n\n**Key Regulatory Thresholds:**\n- 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead primary, neutral, and secondary conductors\n- 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n- 16 feet minimum vertical clearance for driveways/parking without truck traffic\n- 18 feet minimum for roads/streets/alleys with truck traffic\n- Clearances measured from OUTSIDE CONDUCTOR, not pole\n- Service-drop clearances minimum 3-foot above roof (or 18-inch if within 4 feet of roof edge)\n- 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines\n\n**Project Context (Valley View Townhomes):**\n- Located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- 39 townhome units, 8 buildings\n- MF-2 (Multi-Family Medium Density) zoning\n- 2.16 acres (with noted discrepancies down to 2.111 ac)\n- Valley View Road is a Local Street (ASMP Level 1), not highway/freeway\n\n**Critical Applicability Question:**\nThe grouping requires overhead electric facilities to exist on or adjacent to the site. I need to check:\n1. Whether the site has existing overhead electric facilities\n2. What proposed features might be affected\n\nFrom the sheet index (Sheet 21), there is a \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" which suggests electrical infrastructure exists or will be designed. Let me check the facts.md file more carefully and then examine relevant sheets.\n\n\nThe facts.md file references electric easements—specifically two 5-foot electric easements (Easements 7 & 8) and a 7.5-foot public utility easement (Easement 9)—which indicates electrical infrastructure is present or planned on the property. I need to examine the site plan and electrical design sheets to determine the exact location and configuration of overhead lines relative to proposed buildings and site features.\n\nStarting with Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan), Sheet 9 (Site Plan), and Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) should provide the necessary details about utility placement and any constraints they impose on the development.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16434,"cache_read_input_tokens":24713,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16434},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"7af253c8-66fb-4093-86f9-14cc74919b3e"}
