{"level":30,"time":1778264987161,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZhX7aE33mBtSDSbW66QBX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey\" plan, **yes**, there are overhead electric utility lines and utility poles shown.\n\nAccording to the legend located on the left side of the document, overhead electric lines are denoted by a dashed line with the text \"**--- OHE ---**\", and utility poles are denoted by a circle symbol containing a dot.\n\nThese features are primarily located along the property boundaries and right-of-way, relative to the central existing \"SLAB\" (no explicit \"proposed buildings\" are labeled on this existing conditions plan):\n\n*   **Along Valley View Road (Left side of drawing):** Overhead electric lines (`--- OHE ---`) and several utility poles run along the street right-of-way, generally parallel to the `N28°04'28\"E 93.20'` front property line, occasionally crossing it.\n*   **Along the Top Boundary:** An overhead electric line runs roughly parallel to the `S63°02'28\"E 419.86'` property line. It connects to a utility pole near Valley View Road and runs towards the right side of the drawing, appearing to cross slightly inside the property boundary for a section of its length.\n*   **Along the Bottom Boundary:** An overhead electric line runs parallel to the `N63°50'57\"W 414.24'` property line. It appears to be located mostly just outside this property boundary.\n*   **Near the Right Boundary:** There are overhead lines shown near the rear boundary line (`S27°19'28\"W 146.15'`), crossing through the adjacent property labeled \"CLAWSON RIDGE CONDOMINIUMS\".\n\n**Relative to buildings:** Because this is an Existing Conditions Survey, it shows an existing central \"**SLAB**\" footprint rather than proposed buildings. All identified overhead electric lines are located around the outer perimeter of the site (along the boundaries and street frontage) and do not cross over the central existing slab area."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"e997b819-41f3-4b36-95e1-65106b74974e","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey\" plan, **yes**, there are overhead electric utility lines and utility poles shown.\n\nAccording to the legend located on the left side of the document, overhead electric lines are denoted by a dashed line with the text \"**--- OHE ---**\", and utility poles are denoted by a circle symbol containing a dot.\n\nThese features are primarily located along the property boundaries and right-of-way, relative to the central existing \"SLAB\" (no explicit \"proposed buildings\" are labeled on this existing conditions plan):\n\n*   **Along Valley View Road (Left side of drawing):** Overhead electric lines (`--- OHE ---`) and several utility poles run along the street right-of-way, generally parallel to the `N28°04'28\"E 93.20'` front property line, occasionally crossing it.\n*   **Along the Top Boundary:** An overhead electric line runs roughly parallel to the `S63°02'28\"E 419.86'` property line. It connects to a utility pole near Valley View Road and runs towards the right side of the drawing, appearing to cross slightly inside the property boundary for a section of its length.\n*   **Along the Bottom Boundary:** An overhead electric line runs parallel to the `N63°50'57\"W 414.24'` property line. It appears to be located mostly just outside this property boundary.\n*   **Near the Right Boundary:** There are overhead lines shown near the rear boundary line (`S27°19'28\"W 146.15'`), crossing through the adjacent property labeled \"CLAWSON RIDGE CONDOMINIUMS\".\n\n**Relative to buildings:** Because this is an Existing Conditions Survey, it shows an existing central \"**SLAB**\" footprint rather than proposed buildings. All identified overhead electric lines are located around the outer perimeter of the site (along the boundaries and street frontage) and do not cross over the central existing slab area."}]}
