{"level":30,"time":1778265074366,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VkM1c2CYetk1WUqUURubbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have a better picture of what's on Sheet 9. Key features shown:\n\n1. **Buildings**: 8 buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8), with 39 total units\n2. **Driveways**: Yes, shown in site plan\n3. **Parking**: 10 surface parking spaces + 78 garage parking\n4. **Sidewalks**: Concrete sidewalks shown\n5. **Decomposed granite walkways**: Shown\n6. **Detention pond**: Yes, in NE area\n7. **Retaining walls**: Yes, mentioned around site perimeter\n8. **Fences**: Note mentions \"Fence Note\" for post holes in Critical Root Zones, suggesting fences are part of the design\n9. **Utility lines**: OHE line shown on southern boundary\n10. **Easements**: Electric easements shown\n11. **Landscape features**: Referenced (Sheet 31)\n\nFrom Block 5, note (d) states: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\" This is important - it acknowledges that electric infrastructure planning is not complete.\n\nNow, let me systematically evaluate the checklist items. I'll start by understanding which items are clearly NOT applicable (n/a) and which ones are applicable and need evaluation.\n\nBased on my research:\n\n**Applicable Items** (Overhead facilities exist and proposed features are present):\n- EL-1.1: Buildings clearance from overhead - APPLICABLE (buildings proposed, OHE lines shown)\n- EL-1.2: Customer facilities radial clearance - APPLICABLE (buildings proposed)\n- EL-1.3: Building projections clearance - APPLICABLE if projections shown\n- EL-1.6: Buildings clearance in ROW - APPLICABLE (Valley View Road has overhead)\n- EL-1.7: Surveyed elevations on building elevations - APPLICABLE if building elevations required\n\n\n- EL-1.8: Section/plan exhibits with dimensions - APPLICABLE\n- EL-1.9: Fences clearance - APPLICABLE (fences mentioned in fence note)\n- EL-1.14: Retaining walls clearance - APPLICABLE (retaining walls shown)\n- EL-1.18: Driveways clearance - APPLICABLE (driveways shown)\n- EL-1.23: Clearance dimensions measured from conductor - APPLICABLE\n- EL-1.25: Sidewalks and power poles - APPLICABLE (sidewalks shown along frontage)\n- EL-1.31: Survey by registered surveyor - APPLICABLE if vertical clearances marginal\n- EL-1.36\n\n: Decorative lighting - APPLICABLE if lighting near overhead lines\n- EL-1.37: Trees near overhead lines - APPLICABLE (landscape plan exists)\n- EL-1.46: 48-hour notification note - APPLICABLE (overhead lines exist)\n\nSeveral items don't apply since they involve features not included in the proposal: gas pump canopies, elevated structures, fence posts, substations, transmission lines, and vehicle barriers are all absent from the design. N/A unless shown\n- EL-1.28: Water meters clearance - N/A unless shown\n- EL-1.29: Water lines clearance - N/A unless shown\n- EL-1.30: Foundations near property line - N/A unless within 5 feet\n- EL-1.32: Overhead line crossings at 90 degrees - N/A (not new lines)\n- EL-1.33: Secondary over primary crossing - N/A (not applicable)\n- EL-1.34: Marquee signs - N/A (no marquee signs)\n- EL-1.35: New power poles - N/A (no new poles)\n- EL-1.38: Meter locations obstructed - N/A unless meters shown conflicted\n- EL-1.39: Buildings near streetlights - N/A unless shown\n- EL-1.40: Down guy wires conflict - N/A unless present\n- EL-1.41: Guy easements - N/A (not transmission)\n- EL-1.42: Down guy anchor easements - N/A unless shown\n- EL-1.43: Transformers clearance - N/A unless overhead shown\n- EL-1.44: Transformers in niche - N/A unless applicable\n- EL-1.45: Construction staging clearance - N/A or different review\n- EL-1.47: Service-mast installations - N/A unless shown\n\nThe critical issue is that clearance dimensions from overhead electric cond