{"level":30,"time":1778265074366,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEok7KCL7X3oGeStXgBbMj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n     2→\n     3→Plan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n    11→* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n    12→* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n    13→* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n    14→* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n    15→* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n    16→* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n    17→* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n    18→* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n    19→* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n    20→* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    23→\n    24→* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n    25→* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n    26→* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n    27→* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n    28→* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n    29→* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n    30→* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n    31→* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"30078814-5888-46ce-9721-a2ecf220d401","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n\nPlan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778265074366,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CD7qpP7twA3PEMQGwyzLxc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 39 — Wall Plan Details And Notes\n     2→\n     3→Details and cross-sections for multiple pond retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains structural cross-sections and reinforcement details for pond retaining walls of varying maximum heights. Its primary purpose is to provide the exact dimensional, material, and reinforcement specifications required for constructing these walls, alongside soil bearing data and a post-tensioning stressing chart.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→* Max Pond Wall Heights detailed: 4'-0\", 6'-0\", 8'-0\", and 13'-0\"\n    11→* Soil Bearing Pressure: 2000 PSF\n    12→* Geotextile specification: Mirafi 140N Geotextil (or approved equal)\n    13→* Topsoil depth requirement: 12\"\n    14→* Drainage specification (13' wall): 3\" PVC pipe to daylight @ .5% slope\n    15→* 13'-0\" Wall Footing width: 8'-0\" total (2'-9\" heel, 1'-0\" wall, 4'-3\" toe)\n    16→* 13'-0\" Wall Vertical Reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C. Vert. X (minimum 36\" lap for dowels)\n    17→* 4'-0\" Wall Footing width: 3'-1\" total (1'-2 1/2\" heel, 8\" wall, 1'-2 1/2\" toe)\n    18→* Wall Opening Reinforcement: (4) #5 x 4'-0\" bars each face at opening\n    19→\n    20→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    21→\n    22→* **Block 5:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 13'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for the spatial layout of the 8'-0\" footing and drainage pipe location, and READ for heavy reinforcement specifications like the #7 @ 10\" O.C. vertical bars and chamfer notes.\n    23→* **Block 2:** diagram — Cross-section detail of an 8'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for footing dimensions and structural geometry, and READ for reinforcement schedules (#3 and #4 bars) and gravel backfill placement.\n    24→* **Block 4:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 6'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for spatial layout of the 10\" thick wall and footing, and READ for exact rebar spacing and soil layer notes.\n    25→* **Block 1:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 4'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION to examine the basic footing layout, and READ for specific reinforcement sizes (#4 vertical, #3 horizontal) and required dimensions.\n    26→* **Block 3:** diagram — Elevation view of a Typical Opening in Wall Detail. Use VISION to see the diagonal placement of reinforcement around the diamond opening, and READ for the exact bar specification (ADD (4) #5 X 4'-0\").\n    27→* **Block 8:** table — Soil Data Parameters. READ the block content for foundational constraints, specifically the 2000 PSF bearing pressure and source lab information.\n    28→* **Block 9:** table — Post-Tensioning Stressing Chart. READ for the scheduled tabular data mapping cable lengths (15' to 148') to their corresponding elongation requirements (1\" to 11 1/2\").\n    29→* **Blocks 6, 7, 10, 11, 12:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. READ for project identification (3759 Valley View / Pecan Valley Homes), Sheet name (Wall Plan Details and Notes, 39 of 39), MLAW Engineers contact info, and the PE seal/signature.\n    30→\n    31→---\n    32→\n    33→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    34→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"d344913c-01ae-40b1-8105-dedac9b3b6d7","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-39/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 39 — Wall Plan Details And Notes\n\nDetails and cross-sections for multiple pond retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains structural cross-sections and reinforcement details for pond retaining walls of varying maximum heights. Its primary purpose is to provide the exact dimensional, material, and reinforcement specifications required for constructing these walls, alongside soil bearing data and a post-tensioning stressing chart.\n\n**Key values:**\n* Max Pond Wall Heights detailed: 4'-0\", 6'-0\", 8'-0\", and 13'-0\"\n* Soil Bearing Pressure: 2000 PSF\n* Geotextile specification: Mirafi 140N Geotextil (or approved equal)\n* Topsoil depth requirement: 12\"\n* Drainage specification (13' wall): 3\" PVC pipe to daylight @ .5% slope\n* 13'-0\" Wall Footing width: 8'-0\" total (2'-9\" heel, 1'-0\" wall, 4'-3\" toe)\n* 13'-0\" Wall Vertical Reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C. Vert. X (minimum 36\" lap for dowels)\n* 4'-0\" Wall Footing width: 3'-1\" total (1'-2 1/2\" heel, 8\" wall, 1'-2 1/2\" toe)\n* Wall Opening Reinforcement: (4) #5 x 4'-0\" bars each face at opening\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n* **Block 5:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 13'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for the spatial layout of the 8'-0\" footing and drainage pipe location, and READ for heavy reinforcement specifications like the #7 @ 10\" O.C. vertical bars and chamfer notes.\n* **Block 2:** diagram — Cross-section detail of an 8'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for footing dimensions and structural geometry, and READ for reinforcement schedules (#3 and #4 bars) and gravel backfill placement.\n* **Block 4:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 6'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION for spatial layout of the 10\" thick wall and footing, and READ for exact rebar spacing and soil layer notes.\n* **Block 1:** diagram — Cross-section detail of a 4'-0\" Max Pond Wall. Use VISION to examine the basic footing layout, and READ for specific reinforcement sizes (#4 vertical, #3 horizontal) and required dimensions.\n* **Block 3:** diagram — Elevation view of a Typical Opening in Wall Detail. Use VISION to see the diagonal placement of reinforcement around the diamond opening, and READ for the exact bar specification (ADD (4) #5 X 4'-0\").\n* **Block 8:** table — Soil Data Parameters. READ the block content for foundational constraints, specifically the 2000 PSF bearing pressure and source lab information.\n* **Block 9:** table — Post-Tensioning Stressing Chart. READ for the scheduled tabular data mapping cable lengths (15' to 148') to their corresponding elongation requirements (1\" to 11 1/2\").\n* **Blocks 6, 7, 10, 11, 12:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. READ for project identification (3759 Valley View / Pecan Valley Homes), Sheet name (Wall Plan Details and Notes, 39 of 39), MLAW Engineers contact info, and the PE seal/signature.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}}}
