{"level":30,"time":1778265074368,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hccbaa4kbZUuWShYEx4qXZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a precise visual analysis of the provided electrical plan:\n\n**Are transformer easements shown or labeled on the electrical plan?**\nNo, there are no specific areas labeled as a \"Transformer Easement.\" However, the physical equipment is labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** in five distinct locations across the site:\n*   Top left, near Unit 101\n*   Middle left, near Unit 201\n*   Bottom left, near Unit 801\n*   Middle right, near Unit 504\n*   Bottom right, near Unit 704\n\n**What are the widths and locations of any electrical or equipment easements indicated?**\nThe plan does not explicitly label any \"electrical easement\" or \"equipment easement\" with specific widths, but it does show the following related utility easements:\n\n1.  **\"Vault Easement\"**: Located on the middle-left side of the plan, immediately below the labels for \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" and \"Electrical Meters\" (near Unit 801 and Bldg. 8). It points to a dashed rectangular boundary surrounding the equipment. **No width is indicated** for this vault easement.\n2.  **\"5' P.U.E. & Tele. Easement\"**: Located along the bottom-right property boundary (Public Utility and Telephone Easement). The width is explicitly stated as **5' (feet)**.\n3.  **General Public Utility Easements (P.U.E.)**: While not exclusively \"electrical,\" general P.U.E.s which typically house such utilities are labeled along the boundaries:\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E.\"** is labeled along the top boundary.\n    *   **\"5' Public Utility Easement\"** is labeled along the right-side boundary. \n\nAdditionally, an **\"Underground Electric Line\"** is labeled on the left side (outside the main property boundary, near the \"Sid