{"level":30,"time":1778265103280,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018zkkDtr6adXrSStBBCzcRR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grading plan (Sheet 11) and conveyance cross-sections (Sheet 17) show drainage-related profiles but do not appear to include overhead electric line elevations or clearance dimensions.\n\nNow I have enough information to systematically evaluate the checklist. Let me organize my findings:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY — NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n\n1. **No Building Elevation Sheets**: The site plan set includes 39 sheets but contains NO building elevation sheets. Therefore:\n   - EL-1.7: Surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets - CANNOT VERIFY (no such sheets exist)\n   - EL-1.3: Building projections clearance - CANNOT VERIFY (no elevations showing projections)\n\n2. **No Clearance Dimensions on Site Plan**: Despite overhead electric lines being shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and the site plan (Sheet 9), NO horizontal clearance dimensions are provided from the overhead conductors to any proposed buildings, structures, or other facilities.\n\n3. **Overhead Utilities Shown But Not Fully Documented**:\n   - OHE lines shown along south property line and east property line\n   - Electric easements shown (5' and 15')\n   - No pole locations, conductor heights, or vertical clearances documented\n\n4. **No Profile/Section Views with Conductor Elevations**: No grading profiles or cross-sections show overhead conductor elevations in relation to proposed building heights, driveway grades, or parking elevations.\n\n5. **No Utility Plans Showing Existing Overhead Details**: Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows PROPOSED underground utilities, not EXISTING overhead facilities. Existing overhead utilities are not detailed on any plan sheet.\n\n6. **Limited Landscape Plan Review Needed**: Must check Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) to verify tree placement distances from overhead conductors per ECM requirements.\n\n7. **No Service-Mast Elevations**: No indication of service mast installations or roof clearances.\n   \n8. **Notification Requirement**: Need to verify whether the required 48-hour notification note appears on the cover sheet or within the general notes section.\n\nI should review the Landscape Plan and examine the cover sheet and general notes to confirm the notification requirement is documented.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_read_input_tokens":62839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2520},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"a74f73db-fc91-4564-9a67-86d498435ec6"}
