{"level":30,"time":1778265125070,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014uz3b8qcSq24gKXFcr7Ykq","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided document, there are notes requiring 48-hour advance notification to Austin Energy and adherence to Texas state laws regarding overhead power lines, though they do not explicitly cite the exact text \"Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752\". \n\nHere are the exact quotes addressing these requirements:\n\n**Under \"Electric Transmission Notes\":**\n*   **Note 3:** \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Henry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n**Under \"Electric Notes\" (and repeated in an unnumbered paragraph in the center column):**\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\""}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"2606e60c-491a-4907-97f2-67e324fe1989","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided document, there are notes requiring 48-hour advance notification to Austin Energy and adherence to Texas state laws regarding overhead power lines, though they do not explicitly cite the exact text \"Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752\". \n\nHere are the exact quotes addressing these requirements:\n\n**Under \"Electric Transmission Notes\":**\n*   **Note 3:** \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Henry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n**Under \"Electric Notes\" (and repeated in an unnumbered paragraph in the center column):**\n*   **Note 4:** \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\""}]}
