{"level":30,"time":1778265160429,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013zenc4snE9tuAQGTi5AnhU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n     2→\n     3→## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n     4→\n     5→IRRIGATION NOTES:\n     6→AUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n     7→\n     8→1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\n     9→a. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\n    10→b. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\n    11→c. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\n    12→d. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\n    13→e. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\n    14→f. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\n    15→g. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\n    16→h. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n    17→\n    18→2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\n    19→a. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n    20→\n    21→3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\n    22→a. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n    23→\n    24→4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f666cf7-dbf6-4548-8f91-8b523a890b64","uuid":"0eba71f3-76e2-4ce3-95db-c1ed793f7ce1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/block-3.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n\n## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n\nIRRIGATION NOTES:\nAUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\na. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\nb. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\nc. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\nd. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\ne. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\nf. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\ng. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\nh. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n\n2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\na. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n\n3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\na. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n\n4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778265160429,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_017RjNZiAb2kZs2p6WzkG4JT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This block contains irrigation notes, not tree species identification. So I've confirmed that the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) does not identify tree species on the plan itself - only shows them as \"M\" (Mitigation Trees).\n\nNow let me finalize my analysis. I have enough information to make determinations on the checklist items. Let me think through each one carefully:\n\n**Step 3 Research Summary:**\n1. **Overhead Electric Infrastructure**: OHE (Overhead Electric) line is shown along the southern boundary of the site on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)\n2. **Utility Poles**: Marked with \"x\" symbols along the OHE line\n3. **Underground Electric Infrastructure**: Transformers, pull boxes, and underground lines shown on Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21)\n4. **Proposed Trees**: \n   - 2 Live Oak (large trees, 40+ feet mature)\n   - 10 Cedar Elm (large trees, 40+ feet mature)\n   - 6 Mexican Redbud (medium, ~25-30 feet)\n   - 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (medium, ~20-25 feet)\n   - Various shrubs and groundcovers\n5. **Species Identification**: Trees near OHE on Landscape Plan are NOT identified by species - only labeled as \"M\" (Mitigation Tree)\n6. **Clearance Measurements**: NO dimension lines or measurements between trees and OHE line are shown on the Landscape Plan\n7. **Plant Legend**: Sheet 31 has a key notes legend but does NOT identify proposed trees by species\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Specific species identification for trees shown near OHE line on Landscape Plan\n- Clearance dimensions between proposed trees and OHE conductor\n- Identification of which trees are \"large trees\" (40+ feet)\n- Utility compatibility status of any proposed trees\n- Location or dimensions of trees relative to utility poles\n\n\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment\n\nNow I can evaluate each checklist item based on what I've found.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":67560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":938},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f666cf7-dbf6-4548-8f91-8b523a890b64","uuid":"c5ae9f57-b47c-4576-b32b-73e02be9e83e"}
