ing at the south property boundary (determined by the North arrow in the bottom right corner pointing upwards), there is a solid line clearly labeled \"**OHE**\" running horizontally near the bottom edge of the drawing.\n\nBased on a visual analysis of this plan, there are **no tree symbols shown directly along, under, or immediately adjacent** to the path of the overhead electric (OHE) line on the south property boundary.\n\nFor precise context regarding the closest trees to that southern boundary line:\n\n1.  **Southwest Area:** There is a large, existing tree symbol (indicated by concentric circles and dashed canopy lines). This tree is located north of the OHE line. The OHE line passes to the south, entirely outside the drawn canopy of this tree.\n2.  **Southeast Area:** Near the southeast corner of the property, there is a cluster of three tree symbols located inside (north of) a line marked with 'x's (indicated in KEY NOTES as \"H.6 WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"). These trees are distinctly set back from the outer boundary line labeled \"OHE\". These specific tree symbols are accompanied by the text label \"**M**\". The legend below the Key Notes defines \"**M - MITIGATION TREE**\"."}]}
