{"level":30,"time":1778265200696,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Thy16YwijLLDydpDJ5LqkA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've successfully provided the structured output with all findings. Let me summarize what was submitted:\n\n**FAIL Items (2):**\n1. EL-2.10 - Plant legend doesn't identify species (trees near OHE labeled only as \"M\")\n2. EL-2.11 - Large trees not differentiated on plans (all trees shown same way)\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items (9):**\n1. EL-2.1 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution (species not identified)\n2. EL-2.3 - Large trees within 25 ft of distribution (size not differentiated)\n3. EL-2.6 - Trees within 10 ft of pole (no clearance dimensions)\n4. EL-2.8 - Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment (relationship unclear, no dimensions)\n5. EL-2.9 - Root barriers for trees within 20 ft of underground equipment (not shown)\n6. EL-2.12 - Clearance measurement methodology (no measurements shown)\n7. EL-2.13 - Clearance reference point (no measurements shown)\n8. EL-2.15 - Austin Energy approval for prohibited zones (cannot determine applicability)\n\n**N/A Items (4):**\n1. EL-2.2 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission (no transmission lines)\n2. EL-2.4 - Large trees within 50 ft of transmission (no transmission lines)\n3. EL-2.5 - Trees in transmission easement (no transmission easement)\n4. EL-2.7 - Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment (no pad-mounted equipment)\n\n**PASS Items (1):**\n1. EL-2.14 - Trees shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead facilities (YES, they are)\n\n\nThe core issue is that the Landscape Plan lacks species identification and size differentiation for trees near electrical infrastructure, which prevents proper verification of clearance compliance. Without this information clearly documented, it's impossible to determine whether the design meets utility safety requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4801,"cache_read_input_tokens":68498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4801},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f666cf7-dbf6-4548-8f91-8b523a890b64","uuid":"db0ee61f-7c8a-4765-8722-fc8e651c4428"}
