{"level":30,"time":1778265209988,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RfpZhKd7X34noHicr7vdVq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The vision check shows that:\n\n1. The landscape plan shown has trees but they are not placed directly under the OHE line on the south boundary\n2. Existing trees are shown north of the OHE line\n3. Mitigation trees ('M') are shown at the southeast corner but appear to be set back from the OHE line\n\nHowever, I notice the vision check says \"Sheet No. 28 of 35\" which doesn't match the reference to Sheet 31 in my prompt or the README. This suggests there might be some confusion about sheet numbering. But regardless, the key finding is that trees are shown on the landscape plan but appear to be positioned away from the OHE line.\n\nNow let me compile my systematic findings for all 47 checklist items. Based on my research, here's what I've determined:\n\n**CONFIRMED FINDINGS:**\n\n1. **Overhead electric facilities EXIST and are SHOWN:**\n   - OHE lines shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4)\n   - OHE lines shown on site plan (Sheet 9)\n   - OHE lines shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n   - Located along south, east, and west property boundaries\n\n2. **Proposed site features that may require clearances:**\n   - 8 buildings proposed\n   - Driveways proposed\n   - Parking areas proposed (10 surface + 78 garage)\n   - Sidewalks proposed\n   - Retaining walls proposed\n   - Fences proposed (fence note references hand-digging post holes)\n   - Landscape features shown\n\n3. **CRITICAL DEFICIENCY - No Clearance Documentation:**\n   - NO horizontal clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to any buildings\n   - NO building elevation sheets (which are typically required to show clearances)\n   - NO surveyed conductor elevations\n   - NO section views showing building/structure to conductor clearances\n   - NO vertical clearance documentation for driveways/parking\n   \n4. The utilities sheets document proposed underground systems rather than existing overhead infrastructure. Sheet 21 includes a disclaimer that existing utility locations are based on record information only and may not reflect actual construction. The 48-hour notification requirement for Austin Energy does appear on Sheet 3 as part of the transmission line notes, though it's limited to transmission facilities specifically. Trees on the landscape plan are positioned away from the overhead lines, but there's no documentation addressing clearance requirements for vegetation management.\n\n5. Moving through the 47 checklist items, several critical deficiencies emerge. Building clearance dimensions from overhead lines are missing entirely—no measurements shown for radial clearance, building projections, or structures within the right-of-way. Building elevation sheets don't exist, making it impossible to verify clearance compliance or surveyed elevations. Section and plan exhibits lack the dimensional details needed to confirm compliance with utility clearance standards.\n\nAdditional items show similar gaps: fence routing relative to overhead lines isn't fully documented, retaining wall clearances have no dimensional support, and driveway vertical clearance documentation is absent. Clearance measurements aren't taken from the outside conductor as required, and there's no registered surveyor data for mid-span vertical clearances. I need to systematically evaluate all 47 items to identify which ones pass, fail, or cannot be verified based on the available documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":73065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"ad173c6a-1cad-453c-b4d0-17c45105e8b4"}
{"level":30,"time":1778265210614,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RfpZhKd7X34noHicr7vdVq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research, I now have sufficient information to evaluate all 47 checklist items. Let me compile my findings systematically:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY:**\n\n**Evidence Found:**\n- Overhead electric (OHE) lines ARE depicted on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4), site plan (Sheet 9), and landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n- OHE lines run along south, east, and west property boundaries\n- 8 buildings, driveways, parking areas, sidewalks, retaining walls, and fences are proposed\n- Electric easements (5' and 15') are shown on plans\n- 48-hour notification note present on Sheet 3 (Electric Transmission Notes)\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n1. NO horizontal clearance dimensions from overhead electric conductors to any proposed buildings or structures\n2. NO building elevation sheets exist in the set (39 sheets total include no elevations)\n3. NO surveyed overhead conductor elevations shown\n4. NO section/profile views showing clearances from conductors to buildings, driveways, or parking areas\n5. NO vertical clearance verification for driveways under OHE lines\n6. Existing utilities shown but \"based upon record information only\" per Sheet 21 utility notes\n7. No evidence of clearance analysis from outside conductor (vs. pole) positioning"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":73065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e",