{"level":30,"time":1778265310080,"pid":48914,"hostname":"Mac.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RfpZhKd7X34noHicr7vdVq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015T7QduaC56nRQa3uUdevDA","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 near OHE lines on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building clearances from overhead electric conductors cannot be verified. While OHE lines are shown on the site plan along property boundaries where buildings are proposed, no horizontal clearance dimensions are provided from the outside conductors to any building faces. No building elevation sheets are included in the submittal to demonstrate compliance with the required 7-foot 6-inch sky-to-ground clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows OHE line along south property boundary and buildings proposed on site; however, no dimension lines show clearance measurements from the OHE line to any building exterior wall or edge.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor. Without clearance dimension annotations or building elevation documentation, compliance cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Customer facilities (buildings) do not demonstrate compliance with 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution conductors. No clearance dimension annotations are provided on site plan or in building elevation documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows 8 buildings and OHE lines marked on property boundaries, but no radial clearance dimensions (measured in all directions from conductor) are shown for any building location.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary and neutral conductors for all customer facilities. Without dimension documentation, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 with projections"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, roofs) are not documented with clearance verification. No building elevation sheets are provided in the submittal to show the spatial relationship between any building projections and overhead electric conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings but contains no building elevation sheets. The 39-sheet set includes site plans, utility plans, grading, walls, and landscape but no building elevations showing projections and their clearances from overhead lines.","reasoning":"Verification of building projection clearances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial) requires elevation views showing projecting elements. The absence of building elevation documentation prevents this verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on this site plan. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets (Sheets 9, 21) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows buildings, utilities, parking, detention pond, and landscaping but no gas pump infrastructure.","reasoning":"The applicability threshold for EL-1.4 is the proposal of gas pump canopies. Since none are proposed, the item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms (beyond standard floor elevation of buildings) are proposed. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings, walkways, parking, and driveways at various grades. No elevated structures beyond building floors are shown.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to 'stairs, elevated walkways, and elevated platforms' as distinct features. Standard building floor elevations and ground-level sidewalks do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near Valley View Road and south property line where overhead utilities exist in adjacent ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed adjacent to Valley View Road (west property line) where overhead electric lines exist in the right-of-way per the existing conditions survey. Clearances from buildings to the ROW-located overhead facilities are not documented with dimension annotations or elevation data.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) shows OHE lines running along Valley View Road frontage (west property boundary). Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows buildings proposed on site but provides no clearance dimensions from building faces to the OHE lines in the adjacent ROW.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from electric facilities, whether on-site or in adjacent ROW. Without dimension documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan submittal. Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead electric conductors cannot be verified because building elevation sheets, which typically document this information, are absent from the 39-sheet set.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set (39 sheets) includes cover, plat, general notes, survey, erosion control, demolition, site plan, fire protection, grading, utilities, drainage, wall plans, construction details, landscape, and addressing. No sheets are dedicated to building elevations showing exterior faces, heights, and conductor clearances.","reasoning":"The requirement specifically mandates surveyed conductor elevations 'on building elevation sheets.' These sheets do not exist in the submittal. The requirement cannot be satisfied without these documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings on site near OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings are not provided. The site plan shows OHE lines and building layouts but contains no dimension annotations measuring clearances from the conductor to any building face or projection.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) confirms OHE line is labeled on the drawing but no dimension lines extend from the OHE line to any building exterior wall, corner, or edge. No cross-sections or enlarged details show conductor-to-building clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"The code explicitly requires 'dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings.' The complete absence of such dimensions constitutes a failure to satisfy this documentation requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences proposed near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence alignments and clearance distances from overhead electric conductors cannot be verified. While the site plan includes a 'Fence Note' regarding hand-digging requirements in Critical Root Zones, no clearance dimensions are shown between fence alignments and overhead electric conductor positions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 includes a Fence Note (Block 3) referencing tree root zone hand-digging, and the site plan indicates fence routing (H.6 WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE symbol shown). However, no dimension annotations show distance from fence to OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates minimum 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance for fences measured from the outside conductor. Without clearance dimension annotations, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While fence routing is referenced on the site plan, specific fence post locations and dimensions relative to overhead electric pole locations are not detailed. Insufficient specificity in the fence design prevents evaluation of this item, which would otherwise be not-verifiable rather than n/a if fence detail were present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan references fences (H.6 WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE) but does not provide detailed post locations or dimension lines from posts to utility pole centers.","reasoning":"The applicability threshold requires 'overhead electric poles exist on or adjacent to site' (met per Sheet 4) and 'fences are proposed' (indicated via fence note). However, the insufficient design detail of fence post locations relative to specific pole locations prevents evaluation as anything other than n/a due to lack of design specificity.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities are adjacent to or on the site. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets shows easements for City drainage, electric easements, and public utility easements, but no substation property boundaries or substation fence references.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences.' No substation is present on or adjacent to this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) are proposed or located on the site. The OHE lines shown are distribution facilities (indicated by the symbol 'OHE' without transmission-specific labeling). Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show distribution-level overhead electric lines labeled 'OHE' and electric easements labeled as 5' and 15', not transmission easements. Sheet 3 notes reference 'Electric Transmission Notes' regarding pre-construction meetings but transmission voltage levels are not assigned to any lines on the site plan.","reasoning":"The requirement applies to 'fencing proposed beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV).' The site's overhead facilities are distribution, not transmission.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing or posts are specifically shown beneath the OHE line on the site plan. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows privacy fencing (H.6 symbol) and retaining walls but does not depict vehicle barrier posts or crash-rated fencing beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when vehicle barrier posts or fencing are proposed beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines.' General privacy fencing does not constitute a vehicle barrier for this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls on site near OHE line on south property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are proposed and shown on site plan and wall detail sheets. However, clearance distances from the outermost edge of retaining walls to the outside conductor of the overhead electric line are not documented with dimension annotations. The wall plan sheets provide structural details but no clearance dimensions from the OHE line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38-39 (Wall Plans) show retaining wall structural cross-sections and plan layout. Sheet 9 shows retaining wall locations relative to OHE line. No dimension lines connect the wall faces to the OHE conductor location.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor. While walls are shown, clearance verification dimensions are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities are adjacent to the proposed retaining walls. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan and wall plans show retaining walls but no substation property boundaries or substation facilities are depicted or referenced.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property.' No substation is adjacent to this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed on the site beyond standard building floors and driveways. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings, parking, driveways, and landscaping but no specialized emergency access bridges or elevated emergency platforms.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to 'emergency access structures such as bridges or elevated platforms.' Standard site infrastructure does not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near OHE line on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section exhibits for retaining walls are provided (Sheets 38-39), but these sections do not include overhead electric conductor elevations or clearance dimension annotations from the outer conductor to the wall faces. The sections show structural design but not clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall section details (Blocks 1-5 on Sheets 38-39) show wall height, footing, reinforcement, and backfill but do not depict overhead conductor lines or clearance measurements.","reasoning":"The requirement specifically mandates 'section views for retaining wall clearance dimension annotations from outer conductor to wall face.' The wall sections lack this overlay.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways on site under OHE line on south property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are proposed and shown on site plan and grading plan. However, vertical clearances from the lowest point of the overhead electric line (including any attachments) to the finished driveway grade are not documented. No section views show mid-span clearance verification for driveways under the OHE line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows driveway routing; Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) shows driveway grades and contours. Neither sheet contains vertical dimension annotations from overhead conductors to driveway surfaces.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires minimum 16 feet vertical clearance for driveways without truck traffic or 18 feet with truck traffic. Without clearance dimensions or mid-span survey data, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are shown beneath the OHE line on the site plan. The 10 surface parking spaces shown are located away from the OHE routing. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows 10 surface parking spaces and 78 garage spaces. The surface parking lot is positioned on the western/central portion of the site, not beneath the OHE line on the southern boundary.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed beneath overhead electric lines.' The parking shown is not beneath the OHE line.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No roads or driveways are proposed or regraded beneath electric transmission lines. The OHE lines shown are distribution facilities, not transmission. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The overhead lines labeled 'OHE' on the site plan are distribution-level facilities. No transmission lines (≥60kV) are shown crossing over proposed roads or driveways.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.14.0 applies only to transmission lines with 30-foot vertical clearance requirements. Distribution lines are governed by different standards.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway grading with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures is proposed. Valley View Road is classified as a Local Street (ASMP Level 1), not a highway or freeway. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md indicates Valley View Road is ASMP Street Level 1 (Local Street), not a highway or freeway. No transmission structures with distribution underbuilt are referenced on the plans.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to 'highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures.' This project involves a local street and no underbuilt distribution scenario.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed driveways shown on the site plan are in direct conflict with existing electric poles such that pole relocation would be required. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles along property boundaries (in right-of-way and adjacent properties). The proposed driveway routing shown on Sheet 9 does not appear to create a direct conflict with pole locations.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when proposed driveways are shown in conflict with or immediately adjacent to existing electric pole locations.' No such conflict is evident from plan review.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed site features near OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimension annotations are provided on the site plans. Critically, the OHE lines are marked but no dimension lines originate from the outside conductor location. The code requirement mandates that all clearance measurements be taken from the outside conductor, not from utility pole centerlines or structures. The complete absence of clearance dimensions prevents assessment of whether any dimensions that might exist are measured correctly.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) legend shows symbols for 'UTILITY POLE' and 'O.H.U.L.' (Overhead Utility Line). The site plan (Sheet 9) shows an 'OHE' line. However, no dimension lines annotate clearances from either the conductor position or pole center.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires clearances 'measured from the **outside conductor**' (measurement methodology section of grouping guide). The complete absence of any clearance dimensions makes this a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles are proposed to be installed beneath the OHE line. While exterior lighting is noted to comply with full cut-off and fully-shielded standards, no streetlight poles are shown on the photometric or site plan. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) includes a lighting note referencing Figure 34 (fully-shielded fixture examples) but does not identify specific streetlight pole locations. Site lighting is to be 'on the building' per the lighting note.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when new streetlight poles are proposed.' No such poles are shown as proposed on the site plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks along Valley View Road frontage at property limits"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are proposed along the property frontage (shown on site plan). Existing power poles are present along Valley View Road (west property line) per the existing conditions survey. However, the specific alignments of proposed sidewalks relative to the existing pole locations at property limits are not documented with dimension annotations or detailed clearance verifications.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows utility poles along Valley View Road frontage. Sheet 9 indicates sidewalk routing but does not provide detailed dimension annotations showing sidewalk setback from existing poles at property limits.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates sidewalk clearance verification from existing power poles 'at each end of property along right-of-way.' Without specific dimension documentation at these property limit locations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No trash enclosures or receptacle locations are shown on the site plan directly beneath the OHE line on the property. Sheet 9 includes general trash collection notes but does not specify trash bin locations under overhead electric facilities. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) references trash collection notes but does not identify specific dumpster or trash bin locations. The site plan layout shows buildings and common areas but no trash areas are labeled beneath the OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when trash enclosures or receptacle locations are shown beneath overhead electric facilities.' No such locations are identified on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed site features within electric easement boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric easements (5' and 15' marked on site plan) are shown on the site plan. The code absolutely prohibits installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities, independent of clearance distances. Additionally, items within electric easements must maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor. Without detailed easement boundary documentation and clearance dimension annotations from conductors, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows '5' Electric Easement' and 'P.U.E.' (Public Utility Easement) labeled on the drawing. However, no dimension lines show clearance from conductors to any proposed features within these easement areas.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 prohibits facilities under/over distribution AND requires 7.5-foot clearance for items within easements. Without dimension documentation, neither requirement can be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No water meter locations are specifically shown on the utility or site plan in proximity to the OHE service line. Utility tap plan (Sheet 20) would normally show meter locations, but without specific meter placement shown near the OHE line on south boundary, this cannot be evaluated. Item is not applicable based on available plan detail.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) and Sheet 20 (Utility Tap Profile) are referenced as providing water and wastewater tap locations. The specific meter locations relative to overhead electric service drops are not detailed in the available block summaries.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when water meter locations are shown and overhead electric service lines exist.' Insufficient detail prevents determination of applicability.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New water lines are shown on the utility plan (proposed private domestic water 2\" HDPE branches per Sheet 21). However, the specific routing of water lines beneath or adjacent to overhead electrical distribution poles is not detailed with clearance dimensions. Without specific documentation of water line routing relative to distribution pole locations, this cannot be evaluated. Applicability is unclear from plan review.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 references water line routing and Sheet 19-20 show utility tap connections. The specific alignment of water lines relative to distribution pole locations is not annotated on available sheets.","reasoning":"Insufficient plan detail prevents clear determination of whether water lines cross distribution poles and whether clearances are documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building foundations are shown on the site plan; however, no structures are indicated to be founded within 5 feet of the property line where electric facilities in adjacent ROW might require clearance space. Item is not applicable based on site plan layout.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building locations set back from property lines. No foundations are indicated to be within 5 feet of property boundary where electric facilities would require clearance access.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when permanent structure foundations are shown within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities exist or are planned in adjacent ROW.' This condition does not appear to be met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways under OHE line; buildings near OHE line on south and east boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed site features (buildings and driveways) are located in proximity to the OHE line. Without documented conductor elevations and site feature elevations with comparison analysis, vertical clearance compliance appears marginal or unverifiable. No survey data from a registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances is provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show building and driveway locations but do not include surveyed overhead conductor elevations or mid-span clearance measurements. The relationship between building heights (documented on Sheet 9 as 33'-1\" to 36'-1\" above MSL) and overhead conductor elevations is not documented.","reasoning":"When vertical clearances appear marginal, UCM § 1.10.3 and standard practice require registered surveyor data for mid-span clearance verification. No such data is provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross proposed or existing roadways. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground electric lines and infrastructure. No new overhead electric line crossings of roads are proposed.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when new overhead electric lines cross proposed or existing roadways.' The project involves underground utilities for the development.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No secondary overhead electric lines crossing over primary overhead electric lines are shown on the utility plans. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans reference existing overhead lines (OHE) and proposed underground lines but do not depict secondary lines crossing over primary lines.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when both secondary and primary overhead electric lines are shown on utility plans' in a crossing configuration. This is not shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows signage compliance notes referencing LDC Chapter 25-10 but does not depict marquee signs. The project is residential multi-family, not a commercial property typically requiring marquee signage.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when marquee signs are proposed.' None are shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are proposed. The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground infrastructure but does not depict new pole locations. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) references underground service and transformers but does not show new power pole installations.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion.' No new poles are shown as proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixtures on buildings or in common areas near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Decorative lighting is referenced in the site plan notes (exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully-shielded per Subchapter E 2.5, reviewed at building plan stage). However, specific decorative lighting fixture locations and their clearances from the OHE line are not documented with clearance verification dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9, Block 1) states 'all site lighting to be located on the building' and 'all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded.' No separate decorative lighting fixtures in common areas are identified relative to the OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 'clearance verification dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) or relocation notes' for decorative lighting near overhead lines. While building-mounted lighting is addressed, no clearance verification from OHE is provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed near OHE line on south property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees (existing and mitigation trees) near the OHE line on the south property boundary. However, the lateral distance from specific tree symbols to the OHE conductor line cannot be confirmed as within or outside the 10-foot lateral clearance requirement for distribution conductors. Tree species identification on the landscape plan is limited to general categories (SY=Street Yard, PL=Parking Lot, P=existing trees, M=Mitigation), which cannot be cross-referenced against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible trees list without detailed plant schedule. Applicability of utility-compatible species restrictions cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols with labels 'M' (Mitigation Tree) near the south boundary where OHE line runs. Vision check indicated trees are 'set back' from the OHE line but exact distances are not dimensioned. Specific species names are not labeled on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates trees within 10 feet of distribution conductors be from the Utility Compatible list per ECM Appendix F. Without clearance dimensions and species identification, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No proposed electric meter locations are shown on the site plan in proximity to site features that would create obstruction conflicts. The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) mentions meters but does not detail their locations relative to fences, walls, equipment, or landscaping. Insufficient specificity prevents applicability determination.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) references 'electrical meter' placement and transformer locations but does not provide enlarged detail views with meter location coordinates or surrounding feature obstructions.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when electric meter locations are shown on plans' with specific obstructions identified. Insufficient detail prevents evaluation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings located near existing streetlight poles on Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight poles are likely present along Valley View Road per the existing conditions survey, which shows utility poles along the road frontage. However, clearances from proposed buildings to existing streetlight pole locations are not documented with dimension annotations or setback verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) legend identifies 'LIGHT POLE' symbols and 'UTILITY POLE' symbols. These are present along Valley View Road. Sheet 9 shows buildings set back from the west property boundary but no clearance dimensions are provided from building faces to streetlight pole locations.","reasoning":"Without dimension documentation showing clearances from buildings to streetlight poles, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Potential down guy wires from distribution poles on property boundaries or adjacent properties"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires supporting poles may exist or be implied from the utility poles shown on the existing conditions survey and site plan. However, specific down guy wire locations (anchor points and cable routing) are not explicitly depicted or detailed on the plans. No relocation notes or conversion-to-self-supporting-pole specifications are provided. The grouping guide acknowledges that 'electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans,' making verification difficult. Applicability cannot be determined without explicit down guy wire depiction.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles and includes legend symbols for utility infrastructure. The survey note (Block 8) states this survey was performed 'without the benefit of a current title commitment' and 'there may be easements...not shown or noted hereon.' Down guy wire locations are not explicitly marked.","reasoning":"Down guy conflicts would be visible if guy anchor points and accessible path intersections were documented. Their absence from the plans, combined with the surveyor's disclaimer, prevents confident determination of applicability.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission structure guy easements are required. The overhead facilities on this site are distribution-level, not transmission. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans reference distribution easements (5' and 15') and electric easements, not transmission guy easements. No transmission structures requiring angled guy wires are identified.","reasoning":"Guy easements for transmission structures (10 feet either side plus 50-foot extension) apply only to transmission installations. This site has distribution infrastructure.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchors from distribution poles on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor easements (10 feet wide extending 5 feet past ground entry) are not explicitly depicted or documented on the plat or site plan. Existing utility poles shown on the survey may have down guys, but the specific anchor locations and dedicated easement boundaries are not identified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The survey shows utility poles and references easements but does not specifically identify down guy anchor locations or dedicate down guy easements on the plat.","reasoning":"Without explicit depiction of down guy anchor points and easement boundaries, applicability and compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) are shown in direct proximity to overhead electric lines on the site plan. Proposed transformers are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) but appear to be pad-mounted on the ground, not pole-mounted beneath overhead conductors. Item is not applicable based on plan review.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows transformer pads and underground utilities. No pole-mounted transformers are explicitly identified as being positioned beneath overhead conductors.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) are shown and overhead electric lines exist above or adjacent to transformer locations.' The transformers shown appear to be pad-mounted on the ground, not overhead.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations) are shown on the site plans. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows pad-mounted transformers and pull boxes but does not reference niche-type installations with structure covers.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when transformers or switchgears are shown in niche service configurations.' No such configurations are proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, or work platforms are shown on the site plan or construction logistics plan (not provided in site plan set). The temporary OSHA working clearance requirement (10-foot radial from energized lines) would be a construction-phase requirement, separate from permanent facility clearances documented in the site plan. Item is not applicable to permanent site plan review.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set does not include a construction logistics plan showing staging areas, crane swing radius, or equipment laydown zones. This requirement applies to construction documents, not site plans.","reasoning":"OSHA working clearances during construction are enforced through construction documents and contractor safety protocols, not permanent site plans. This item is typically not evaluated at the site plan review phase.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["General Notes cover sheet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The required 48-hour notification note to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines is present on Sheet 3 (General Notes). The note (Electric Transmission Notes, Note 3) states: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.' This satisfies the requirement for owner/contractor notification per Texas state law.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 3 confirmed that Electric Transmission Notes include Note 3: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153...'","reasoning":"The requirement mandates a note that 'owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.' The 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting requirement satisfies this mandate.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are shown on the site plan or building elevation sheets. The project is a multi-family townhome development with individual units served by underground electrical service (per Sheet 21 electrical design plan). Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground electric lines serving building meters. No through-roof service mast installations are depicted.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only 'when service-mast through-roof installations are shown on building elevations.' These are not proposed.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":73065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9306442-64b4-48d1-9fb6-43ef93edac6e","uuid":"dde17097-eebb-4be1-818c-e83c21b2fc67"}
