e 30-word target. The first detail should focus on the missing relationship between underground equipment and tree locations without clearance dimensions. The second should emphasize the landscape plan's failure to identify trees in the equipment protection zone and lack root barrier specs. Both reference UCM § 1.10.10.4. Now I'm ready to format the JSON output with the proper runComments structure. not identified by species on the Landscape Plan. Unable to confirm compliance with utility clearance requirements for non-compatible species within 15 feet of the conductor.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"runNum\": 2,\n              \"status\": \"fail\",\n              \"comment\": \"Species identification missing for all mitigation trees. This is a critical gap since certain species are prohibited within utility corridors per Austin Energy standards.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Mature height and clearance dimensions from conductor and poles are not provided for any proposed trees. Cannot verify compliance with minimum clearance requirements.\",\n          \"citation\": \"UCM § 1.10.10.4, Austin Energy Design Standards\",\n          \"sourceId\": \"2:EL-2.2\",\n          \"confidence\": 3,\n          \"runComments\": [\n            {\n              \"runNum\": 1,\n              \"status\": \"nv\",\n              \"comment\": \"No mature height data or clearance measurements provided for trees near overhead lines. Required for utility approval.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"runNum\": 2,\n              \"status\": \"fail\",\n              \"comment\": \"Height and clearance information is essential documentation. Without it, cannot assess whether trees will maintain safe distances from conductors as they mature.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe landscape plan shows mitigation trees near the overhead electric line but lacks critical specificatio