nting verification of overhead clearance compliance.","citation":"Reviewer Convention; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.11","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees proposed on the Landscape Plan are not differentiated from smaller trees by size, caliper, mature height, or any visual or textual designation. All mitigation and proposed trees are shown with the same symbol regardless of their mature height. Differentiation is required to allow reviewers to verify that large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) comply with clearance restrictions from overhead electric facilities."}]},{"text":"No tree clearance measurements or dimensions are shown on Landscape Plan between proposed trees and overhead electric line. Measurement methodology (pole centerline vs. conductor, trunk center vs. canopy edge) cannot be assessed due to absence of dimensions.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.12","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No tree clearance measurements or dimensions are shown on the Landscape Plan between proposed trees and the overhead electric line. Therefore, the measurement methodology (whether measured from pole centerline vs. conductor, or from trunk center vs. canopy edge) cannot be assessed. This item is not verifiable due to absence of measurements rather than incorrect measurement methodology."}]},{"text":"No tree clearance dimensions on Landscape Plan prevent evaluation of whether measurements reference tree trunk center or canopy edge. Item is not verifiable due to absence of measurements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.13","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No tree clearance measurements are dimensioned on the Landscape Plan, so the measurement reference point (tree trunk center vs. canopy edge) cannot be evaluated. This checklist item cannot be verified due to the absence of measurements rather than incorrect methodology."}]},{"text":"Without species identification and clearance dimensions on Landscape Plan, cannot determine whether proposed trees are within prohibited clearance zones from overhead line. Austin Energy written approval for variations, if required, cannot be verified or documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.15","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Without species identification for trees on the Landscape Plan and without clearance dimensions, it cannot be determined whether any proposed trees are within prohibited clearance zones. Therefore, the presence or absence of Austin Energy written approval for variations cannot be assessed. If trees are determined to be within restricted zones, such approval would be required and must be documented on the plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Underground equipment trees lack clearance and barrier details","summary":"Proposed trees near underground electrical equipment (transformers and pull boxes shown on Sheet 21) lack clearance dimensions on the Landscape Plan and have no root barrier specifications. Cannot verify required clearances and root protection in the 20-foot utility equipment zone.","sheets":[21,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Utility department (cross-sheet equipment coordination); Landscape architect (plan coordination)","attn":"Verify coordination between Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) showing equipment locations and Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) showing tree locations with required clearance dimensions.","details":[{"text":"Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground equipment (transformers and pull boxes), but relationship to proposed tree locations on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) is not clearly depicted. No clearance dimensions provided between equipment and tree locations.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground electric equipment (transformers and pull boxes) is shown on the Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), but the relationship between these equipment locations and the proposed tree locations on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) is not clear. No clearance dimensions are shown between underground equipment and proposed trees."}]},{"text":"Landscape Plan does not indicate which trees are within 20-lateral-foot zone of underground equipment, nor does it show required root barrier specifications (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.9","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"The Landscape Plan does not indicate which proposed trees are within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, nor does it show root barrier specifications. Cannot verify required root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) for trees within the 20-foot zone."}]}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14196,"cache_read_input_tokens":26670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14196},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93aaff38-86d3-454a-9195-13e28acbfb61","uuid":"a555ddb7-b4e2-4131-8fad-05e872ba6141"}
